  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The fix is one line in `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py`.\n\nA child context was inheriting the parent's whole `default_map`. A map like `{'runserver': {'port': 5000}}` was therefore searched for `port` at the top level, and nothing matched. The child now uses `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, which is the nested lookup `docs/commands.md` describes.\n\nThe existing test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't add a regression test for the nested subcommand case, so nothing in the suite exercises it directly.",
